.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/loose-envify Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "loose-envify"
.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
Fast (and loose) selective \fRprocess\&.env\fP replacer using \fRjs-tokens\fP instead of an AST\&. Works just like \fRenvify\fP but much faster\&.
.SH "Gotchas"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Doesn't handle broken syntax\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Doesn't look inside embedded expressions in template strings\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBthis won't work:\fP 
.PP
.nf
console\&.log(`the current env is ${process\&.env\&.NODE_ENV}`);

.fi
.PP

.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
Doesn't replace oddly-spaced or oddly-commented expressions\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBthis won't work:\fP 
.PP
.nf
console\&.log(process\&./*won't*/env\&./*work*/NODE_ENV);

.fi
.PP

.PP

.PP
.SH "Usage/Options"
.PP
loose-envify has the exact same interface as \fRenvify\fP, including the CLI\&.
.SH "Benchmark"
.PP
.PP
.nf
envify:

  $ for i in {1\&.\&.5}; do node bench/bench\&.js 'envify'; done
  708ms
  727ms
  791ms
  719ms
  720ms

loose\-envify:

  $ for i in {1\&.\&.5}; do node bench/bench\&.js '\&.\&./'; done
  51ms
  52ms
  52ms
  52ms
  52ms
.fi
.PP
 
